# Editor lives in the main column

The workspace **stage** (`.stage-col`, the wide column beside the area rail) is the editor for scene and library item contents. Shared requirements: [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md).

## Do this

- Open **scenes**, **variables**, **palettes**, and **circadian themes** in that column (`#edit/<id>`, `#variable/<id>`, `#variable/new`, `#palette/<id>`, `#palette/new`, `#theme/<id>`, `#theme/new`).
- Create and edit them there (name, color wheel, palette slots, theme dial). Autosave like other editors.

## Do not

- Creation dialogs may choose a starter or existing preset, then create the item and open the stage. Do not put name/color/slot/theme editing in `ha-dialog` / `_libraryDialog`. Rename, settings, confirmations, and light sidebars remain supporting surfaces.
- Do not use a separate full-page library column as the editor (the rail stays a picker).

Rationale: [`docs/DECISIONS.md`](../../docs/DECISIONS.md) (“Main column is the editor”).
